### Tested versions

- Reproducible in Godot v4.5.1.stable.official [f62fdbde1]

### System information

Godot v4.5.1.stable - Fedora Linux 43 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1080 (nvidia; 580.119.02) - AMD Ryzen 5 3500 6-Core Processor (6 threads) - 15.53 GiB memory

### Issue description

Good day

When adding documentation to a shader using `/** ... */` does not show in the inspector for arrays defined in the shader.

```gdshader
shader_type spatial;

/** test1 */
uniform int test1;

/** test2 */
uniform int test2[3];

void vertex() {
	// Called for every vertex the material is visible on.
}

void fragment() {
	// Called for every pixel the material is visible on.
}

//void light() {
//	// Called for every pixel for every light affecting the material.
//	// Uncomment to replace the default light processing function with this one.
//}

```

<img width="1145" height="645" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6b5b0b2c-bf9d-4858-a044-6dd112f4b56a" />

### Steps to reproduce

- Create a Godot shader
- Add a uniform array of any type
- Add documentation for the array using `/** */`
- Hover over the array in the inspector

